course: dictionary
lesson: 9459
title: A word for a person who stares
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A starer is a person who stares. Stare means to look at someone or something for a long time with fixed eyes. Starer is a rare word, so people often say «someone who stares» instead.
explain: Context gives the clues. «Arjun keeps staring at Lily and whispering» shows a long, fixed look. Lily thinks he is plotting, but his mate says, «He fancies you, he's just a bit of a muppet about it.» Fancies means likes, and a muppet is a daft, silly person, so Arjun is being silly, not nasty.
explain: Staring can make people feel uncomfortable or hurt, especially when they look different from others. If someone is staring at you, do not stare back. Smile, say hello, or look away. Not every starer is an enemy, and a kind hello can change how a stare feels.
fact: A starer is a noun: a person who stares.
fact: Stare means to look at someone or something for a long time with fixed eyes.
fact: «Starer» is a rare word; people usually say «someone who stares».
fact: Staring at people who look different can make them feel uncomfortable or hurt.
fact: «Muppet» is British slang for a silly, daft person, and «fancies» means likes someone.
exercise: In «Arjun keeps staring at Lily and whispering», who is the starer? | The teacher | *Arjun | Arjun's mate | Lily
exercise: What does starer mean? | A person who runs very fast | A person who shines in the dark | *A person who stares for a long time with fixed eyes | A person who tells lies
exercise: What is a kind thing to do if someone is staring at you? | Stare back until they stop | Hide under the table | *Smile or say hello | Shout at them loudly
test: What does «fancies» mean in «he fancies you»? | Copies | Ignores | Hates | *Likes
test: Why might Arjun's staring be less scary than Lily thinks? | *Because he is just being a bit silly about liking her | Because he is trying to scare her | Because he is copying a film | Because he wants her homework
exam: In «Not every starer is an enemy», what does enemy mean? | A teacher at school | *A person who is against you or wants to harm you | A person who wins races | A friend who lives nearby
